---
import Ichthys from './icons/Ichthys.astro';
import IconTooltip from './IconTooltip.astro';

const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/scryptoginger/sumbible';
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="border-t border-stone-300">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-10 text-sm text-stone-500">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr] md:gap-10">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2">
          <span class="font-semibold text-stone-700">SumBible</span>
          <a href="/about" class="hover:text-accent">About</a>
          <a href="/christ" class="hover:text-accent">Christ</a>
          <a href="/themes" class="hover:text-accent">Themes</a>
          <a href="/related-texts" class="hover:text-accent">Related&nbsp;Texts</a>
          <a href="/cross-references" class="hover:text-accent">Cross-references</a>
          <a href={repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:text-accent">GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <p class="max-w-prose text-stone-500">
          SumBible is a study aid, not a replacement for personal scripture reading.
          Most content is AI-generated and should be considered in that context.
          Summaries link out to canonical editions for the scripture text itself.
        </p>
        <span class="text-stone-400">© {year}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center self-center md:px-4">
        <IconTooltip
          title="Ichthys"
          description="Greek for 'fish' (ΙΧΘΥΣ); an early Christian acronym for Iēsous Christos Theou Hyios Sōtēr (Jesus Christ, Son of God, Savior)."
          learnMoreHref="/about/iconography/ichthys"
        >
          <Ichthys size={48} class="text-stone-300" />
        </IconTooltip>
      </div>
      <aside class="self-center">
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
          You have a Heavenly Father and He is your Creator. He loves you! He
          sent His Son, Jesus Christ, to do what you cannot do for yourself so
          you can return to Him after death. You can speak to Him through
          humble prayer &mdash; He hears you and He <em>listens</em>. He will
          answer you, too, if you listen.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
